      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:93:5",
      "text": [
        " الْمُحْرِمُ لَا يَكْتَحِلْ إِلَّا مِنْ وَجَعٍ وَ قَالَ لَا بَأْسَ بِأَنْ تَكْتَحِلَ وَ أَنْتَ مُحْرِمٌ بِمَا لَمْ يَكُنْ فِيهِ طِيبٌ يُوجَدُ رِيحُهُ فَأَمَّا لِلزِّينَةِ فَلَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Muawiya, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span> cannot apply Kohl except for pain’. And he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is no problem with if you apply Kohl and you are in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span>, with what does not happen to have perfume in it or its aroma is not found. But, as for adornment, so no’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Mu‘awiyah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘One in the state of Ihram must not use kohl unless it is to cure pain.’ He (the Imam) has said, ‘Using kohl which does not have any perfume while one is in the state of Ihram is not harmful, however, for beautification it is not permissible.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
